From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "mayuresh.wani" <mayuresh.wani@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:49:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: soc: mediatek: add power_wrap device power
 control driver

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167298

Add the power_wrap driver: ACPI-driven device power control through
the SSPM control interface. Kernel clients and the ACPI power flows
use it to request device power, clock and mode changes from the SSPM
firmware, which reference counts the requests across operating system
components.

The public client header is introduced directly at
include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk-pwrap.h so in-tree consumers outside
drivers/soc can include it without relative paths.

Signed-off-by: mayuresh.wani <mayuresh.wani@mediatek.com>
